WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.711
An illustrative walkthrough of IBM Bob Shell running the
kit headless: probed, but no stage was run end to end.

2
00:00:04.711 --> 00:00:06.960
Checker results are real; grey bars cover run values.

3
00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:10.868
A customer asks what it will take to modernise
their legacy app, and what it will cost.

4
00:00:10.868 --> 00:00:13.848
Four Bob runs turn their code into
the documents an SI prices from.

5
00:00:13.848 --> 00:00:16.960
We'll follow one bug from the code
all the way to a line in the price.

6
00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:25.960
Each bob run starts Bob in one persona mode, does
one stage, then stops. You check it before the next.

7
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:34.850
First, set up once: open the kit in IBM Bob, trust the
folder, check Python and Bob Shell, and set your API key.

8
00:00:49.660 --> 00:00:54.035
Bob Shell is IBM Bob in your terminal: the bob command.

9
00:00:54.035 --> 00:01:00.000
Check you have Python 3.11 or later for
the checkers, and that bob answers.

10
00:01:06.421 --> 00:01:11.134
Discover. You choose a run name,
acme-1 here, and Bob records evidence:

11
00:01:11.134 --> 00:01:15.780
a file and line for what it read, or
a named gap for what it couldn't.

12
00:02:29.805 --> 00:02:34.021
Assess. Bob turns the evidence into
findings and an assessment report.

13
00:02:34.021 --> 00:02:39.080
Because he can't ask you mid-run, you say
in the prompt that the last checks passed.

14
00:03:18.593 --> 00:03:26.093
Plan. Bob orders the work into packages
and staffs them from the roster.

15
00:04:03.694 --> 00:04:12.611
Price. Bob writes effort rows and a draft
statement of work. Your own tools do the money.

16
00:05:26.939 --> 00:05:29.980
That's the draft pack, ready for senior review.

17
00:05:51.581 --> 00:05:55.573
One line of code, traced to one line of the price.

18
00:05:55.573 --> 00:06:02.041
When the customer asks why the SOW includes
this fix, you can show them the line.

19
00:06:02.081 --> 00:06:12.060
To try it: one bob run per stage, a checker after each.
Try one stage first: no full stage has been run this way.
